{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>For I am YHWH who brings you up, etc.</b> According to Rashi's interpretation, it is difficult: why is this detail specified for this commandment more than for the other commandments? And furthermore, there are several differences between the swarming creeping thing (שֶׁרֶץ הַשּׁוֹרֵץ) and the creeping thing that moves upon the earth (שֶׁרֶץ הָרוֹמֵשׂ עַל הָאָרֶץ), which is more strongly attached to the ground, whose walking is not perceptible. For concerning it, 'upon the earth' is stated, but not concerning the swarming thing; and concerning the one that moves, impurity of the soul is mentioned, as it says: ״וְלֹא תְטַמְּאוּ אֶת נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם״, while concerning the swarming thing it says ״וְלֹא תְשַׁקְּצוּ אֶת נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם״." "Therefore I say, that everything closest to the earth and farthest from the air has a greater share of earthiness (עַפְרוּרִיּוּת) than those that are somewhat elevated from the earth — for it turns and looks toward the source from which it was hewn. And this is the reason that man does not walk on four: for half of him is material and half of him is spiritual, and he faces upward. And the term impurity (טֻמְאָה) is lesser than the term abomination (שִׁקּוּץ), which indicates something detestable to man even though there is no impurity in its essence. Therefore the creeping thing that moves upon the earth and drags along it, whose walking is not perceptible, has a greater share of earthiness; therefore it impurifies the soul more. And since the body is more prone to receive impurity from the soul, therefore concerning the swarming creeping thing, which is somewhat removed from the earth, He said ״אַל תְּשַׁקְּצוּ אֶת נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם״ — for they cause the soul only abomination and not impurity — ״וְלֹא תִטַּמְּאוּ בָהֶם״, that is, the body, which is more prone and also receives the impurity. But the creeping thing that moves upon the earth, which is lesser than it, concerning it is stated: ״וְלֹא תְטַמְּאוּ אֶת נַפְשׁוֹתֵיכֶם״ — and by a fortiori reasoning, all the more so the body, and by a fortiori reasoning, all the more so abomination. And He gave a reason for the matter: ״כִּי אֲנִי ה׳ הַמַּעֲלֶה אֶתְכֶם מֵאֶרֶץ מִצְרַיִם״ — a low place — to the land of Israel, which is higher than all the lands (Zevaḥim 54a) — in order to distance you from the earthiness that dominates more in a low place where the air does not hold sway there as it does in a high place. Therefore you must be more careful regarding the creeping thing that moves upon the earth. And this is a correct and clear reason." "And the reason for slaughter (שְׁחִיטָה) will prove it, for slaughter comes to remove the impurity of the earthiness that is in the animal, which was formed from the earth. But fish, which were formed from water, whose source is purity, do not require slaughter at all, but gathering alone suffices. And birds, which were formed from the mud, a mixture of earth and water, it suffices for them to have one sign to diminish the earthiness that is in them. And as for why water brings impurity upon food, you will find it explained further on, in the portion of Ḥukkat, in the mystery of the red heifer, which impurifies the pure and purifies the impure."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:36:07.528087052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}